; judge-v3.pmp - third cut (2026-10-09, same day; judge.pmp and judge-v2.pmp are unchanged). Change: judge-v2.pmp
; kept the line set ATL const ar at the top of TAUTCHK, which would have pointed the atom table at the last allocation;
; the line is removed. The rest is judge-v2.pmp.
;
; judge-v2.pmp - second cut of judge.pmp (2026-10-09, same day; judge.pmp is unchanged). Changes: the registry copy
; looped to its body (goto REGCOPY1) instead of its test, copied without end and crashed the interpreter; it now
; returns to REGCOPY. The atom table of the tautology check is allocated once at the start instead of 512 KB per
; taut step. The rest is judge.pmp.
;
; judge.pmp - the posting checker of the Book: check_batch of forcing-src/general/Replay2.v, in PmpCore forms only
; (set const/add/sub/mul, set peek, poke, set alloc, text literal, when zero/nonzero/negative, goto, gosub, return,
; label, trace) plus read, text arg, say, show, print and check zero, so that its meaning is the operational semantics
; of PmpCore.v / PmpFull.v. Written 2026-10-09 (first cut).
;
; Run: pompetzki.exe judge.pmp FILE.jdg
; Exit 0 and ACCEPT, or REJECT (a step or a theorem fails) / LIMIT (a resource bound) with a nonzero exit.
;
; What it decides, function for function as in Replay2.v:
;   the registry: a list of (formula, hypothesis numbers); theorems are checked in order and each accepted theorem is
;   appended (check_batch);
;   check_thm: the steps run in order (run / sstep), the last line equals the statement renamed by sig, sig has no
;   repeated number, the statement is closed in length(sig) variables, the hypotheses the steps used are among the
;   theorem's, and there is at least one line;
;   sstep: use spec gen mp taut exi exel alli inst leib ax, with tof (the abbreviations K D Q X expanded), ren under
;   binders (scons, absk, sigf, S, skip1, ins2, unskip), form_eqb, free, closedk, specn, prems, axshape (k s c dist vac
;   refl, Separation and Collection in the shapes isSepN / isCollN), tautchk2 (atoms, then Shannon expansion with the
;   simplifications mkN / mkI).
; Replay3.v proves check_batch sound for prov (Gam with the hypotheses); this program is meant to compute it.
;
; Input format JDG1 (rocq2jdg.rkt writes it from Rocq data; the converter is not trusted):
;   JDG1  R n ENTRY^n  T m THEOREM^m
;   ENTRY   = FORM LIST           THEOREM = FORM LIST(sig) n STEP^n LIST(hyps)          LIST = count then numbers
;   FORM    = e x y | q x y | p P LIST | n F | i F G | a F | k F G | d F G | b F G | x F
;   STEP    = U r LIST | S l LIST | G l k | M i j | T LIST FORM | E t FORM | L l k FORM | H k l FORM | V t FORM
;             | Z FORM FORM | Y FORM
;
; Data: a formula is a node of four words [tag, a, b, c]: 1 Mem x y, 2 Eqv x y, 3 Pr p args n, 4 Neg a, 5 Imp a b,
; 6 All a. A Boolean term of the tautology check is a node 11 BT, 12 BF, 13 BV n, 14 BN a, 15 BI a c.
; Memory: one persistent block (registry statements and hypotheses) and one scratch block reset for every theorem,
; both handed out by ALLOC; a data stack (DSB .. DSE) keeps the locals of the recursive routines across gosub.
; Temporaries t and q are never relied on across a gosub.

; judge-v4.pmp authenticates initial registries against embedded proved REG0.
; Original judge-v3 computation follows authentication; source-v3 is preserved.
trace off
